<p>It was iPhone Duo preorder day, if you didn&#8217;t know. If you weren&#8217;t up at 5 a.m. Pacific like I was. Like so many of us were.</p>
<p>Stephen Hackett (who is traveling today) <a href="https://512pixels.net/2026/10/my-iphone-duo-pre-order-got/">had some bad luck</a>:</p>
<blockquote><p>
  By the time the website came up over six minutes later — where you <em>can</em> search for other Apple Stores — my ship date had already slipped to the end of November or early December.</p>
<p>  It seems that my work on Widgetsmith and our other apps will be constrained to the simulator a little longer. It is also nice to have the new thing when it’s new, so I can write and talk about it when it’s new.</p>
<p>  I guess the upside is that, now that shipping dates have slipped into 2027, the iPhone Duo will be new for a long time.
</p></blockquote>
<p>Clearly Apple is struggling with Duo supply, but there&#8217;s also obviously a lot of Duo demand and curiosity out there. Put them together and you get a device that&#8217;s sold out into next year already. The Duo is not going to be the best-selling iPhone of this cycle—not even close—but I still think it will be the best-selling folding phone ever, and by a lot.</p>
<p>For the record: I got all the way to the final screen with Apple telling me my 256GB Night Sky order would be available next Friday. But then it slipped to Nov 9 – Nov 16.</p>
<p>At least it&#8217;s not January.</p>
